  "summary": "Duplicate Advisory: vLLM 0.7.3 before 0.31.0 DoS via Unvalidated mm_processor_kwargs",
  "details": "## Duplicate Advisory\n\nThis advisory has been withdrawn because it is a duplicate of GHSA-gx7p-2j49-hfq4. This link is maintained to preserve external references.\n\n## Original Description\nvLLM from 0.7.3 before 0.31.0 contains an uncontrolled resource consumption vulnerability that allows remote clients to control multimodal processor parameters by supplying per-request mm_processor_kwargs. Attackers can set large image size, patch count, crop count, or frame count values in Isaac, InternVL, H2OVL, and other processors to exhaust memory and terminate the shared server.",
